# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7
# AI worker. Same image, two commands: `python -m ai_worker.main` (HTTP health) and
# `python -m ai_worker.temporal_worker` (Temporal activities).
FROM python:3.12-slim AS build
COPY --from=ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.8 /uv /usr/local/bin/uv
ENV UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE=1 UV_LINK_MODE=copy
WORKDIR /srv/services/ai-worker
COPY services/ai-worker/pyproject.toml services/ai-worker/uv.lock ./
RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/uv uv sync --frozen --no-dev --no-install-project

FROM python:3.12-slim
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends curl && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* \
 && useradd --create-home --uid 10001 app
WORKDIR /srv/services/ai-worker
COPY --from=build /srv/services/ai-worker/.venv ./.venv
COPY services/ai-worker/src ./src
COPY services/ai-worker/prompts ./prompts
ENV PATH="/srv/services/ai-worker/.venv/bin:$PATH" PYTHONPATH=/srv/services/ai-worker/src \
    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 ENV=production PORT=8000
USER app
EXPOSE 8000
HEALTHCHECK --interval=15s --timeout=3s --start-period=20s CMD curl -fs http://localhost:8000/health || exit 1
CMD ["python", "-m", "ai_worker.main"]
